"                                                                                                                        "
"                                                                                                                        "
"                                                                                                                        "
"                                                                                                                        "
"            ╔════════════════════════════════════════════ Help ════════════════════════════════════════════╗            "
"            ║  About                │ ── Modes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── ▲            "
"            ║  Keys ▾               │ - Keys are vim's, in its modes; the F-keys of the panels are mc's,   █            "
"            ║   Everywhere          │   in Normal and Visual mode and in quick search.                     █            "
"            ║   Panels              │ - Text fields open in Insert mode, where characters are text; Esc    █            "
"            ║   Text fields         │   goes to Normal mode, and Esc there closes.                         █            "
"            ║   Search and renaming │ - Quick search and the command line close on Esc, as vim's search    █            "
"            ║   Command line        │   and command line do.                                               █            "
"            ║   Lists and menus     │ - The line above the F-key bar says the mode, NORMAL, INSERT, or     █            "
"            ║   Menus and dialogs   │   VISUAL, and the window that has the keys, as INSERT · Dialog;      █            "
"            ║   Viewer              │   quick search and the command line are typed there in its place, as ░            "
"            ║   Tips                │   in vim. (insert) is the one command of Normal mode after Ctrl+o.   ░            "
"            ║                       │   The cursor is a bar in Insert mode.                                ░            "
"            ║                       │ - Alt and a key stand for Esc and the key in Insert and Visual mode  ░            "
"            ║                       │   and in the panels, but on a password, and in the dialogs and the   ░            "
"            ║                       │   pull-down menu, where Alt and a highlighted letter act on what has ░            "
"            ║                       │   it.                                                                ░            "
"            ║                       │ - Ctrl+c closes or cancels in every mode.                            ░            "
"            ║                       │                                                                      ░            "
"            ║                       │ ── Counts and registers ──────────────────────────────────────────── ░            "
"            ║                       │ - In Normal mode, a count goes before a command: 5j goes five rows   ░            "
"            ║                       │   down, 3G to the third row, 2g t to the second tab, and d3w deletes ░            "
"            ║                       │   three words.                                                       ░            "
"            ║                       │ - In text fields, "a names a register, which every field shares, and ░            "
"            ║                       │   A appends to it.                                                   ░            "
"            ║                       │                                                                      ░            "
"            ║                       │ ── Lists ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── ░            "
"            ║                       │ - The lists open in Insert mode, typing in the filter: Esc goes to   ░            "
"            ║                       │   the rows, in Normal mode, / types in the filter again, and Esc     ░            "
"            ║                       │   there closes the list.                                             ░            "
"            ║                       │ - In the zoxide window, what is typed filters its directories, or,   ▼            "
"            ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ 30% ═╝            "
